Affected component: Layer-2 VLAN5 uplink on switch4 (subinterface eth0.5, member of bridge br_vlan5).  
Mechanism: PCs in VLAN5 can switch locally among access ports on switch4 (pc1↔pc2↔dc_pc5 pings succeed), but ARP to the default gateway 10.5.0.254 fails because the VLAN5 uplink towards the router-on-a-stick (sshswitch) is down. With no forwarding path out of switch4’s VLAN5 bridge, ARP requests never reach the gateway and remain “incomplete,” causing all off-switch traffic (including to 10.5.0.254) to fail.  
